nt new results and discuss some observations that lead to simple\nproofs of some known cases of the conjecture.\n49--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: Kite graphs determined by their spectra. (https://dblp.uni-trier.de/rec/journals/amc/DasL17.html)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # \"Kite graphs determined by their spectra.\"\n\n# \"Kite graphs determined by their spectra.\"\n\n  * help us\n\n    * How can I correct errors in dblp?\n    * contact dblp\n\nKinkar Chandra Das, Muhuo Liu (2017)\n\n\n## Details and statistics\n\n  * show external API response\n\n    * JSON @ openalex.org\n\nsee also:\n\n    * API doc @ openalex.org\n\nDOI: 10.1016/J.AMC.2016.10.032\n\naccess: closed\n\ntype: Journal Article\n\nmetadata version: 2020-02-21\n\n  * Image: Journal Articles\n\n    * export record\n\n      * BibTeX\n      * RIS\n      * RDF N-Triples\n      * RDF Turtle\n      * RDF/XML\n      * XML\n      * plain text\n\ndblp key:\n\n      * journals/amc/DasL17\n\n    * ask others\n\n      * Google\n      * Google Scholar\n      * Semantic Scholar\n      * Internet Archive Scholar\n      * CiteSeerX\n      * PubPeer\n\n    * share record\n\n      * Bluesky\n      * Reddit\n      * BibSonomy\n      * LinkedIn\n\npersistent URL:\n\n      * https://dblp.org/rec/journals/amc/DasL17\n\nKinkar Chandra Das, Muhuo Liu:\nKite graphs determined by their spectra. Appl. Math. Comput. 297: 74-78 (2017)\n\n\nlast updated on 2020-02-21 21:20 CET by the dblp team\n\n all metadata released as open data under CC0 1.0 license--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNEW FAMILIES OF GRAPHS DETERMINED BY THEIR (https://ueaeprints.uea.ac.uk/id/eprint/69709/1/New_families_of_graphs_determined_by_their_generalized_spectrum.pdf)\nciteturn1search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7.8 years ago; some almost complete graphs [1], pineapple graphs [10] and kite graphs [11]. ... 1Keywords: Graph spectrum, Walk matrix, Graphs determined by generalized spectrum\nNEW FAMILIES OF GRAPHS DETERMINED BY THEIR\nGENERALIZED SPECTRUM\nFENJIN LIU, JOHANNES SIEMONS, WEI WANG\nAbstract: We construct inﬁnite families of graphs that are determined by their gener-\nalized spectrum. This construction is based on new formulae for the determinant of the\nwalk matrix of a graph.\nAll graphs constructed here satisfy a certain extremal divisibility\ncondition for the determinant of their walk matrix.1\n1.\nIntroduction\nLet G be a graph on the vertex set V with adjacency matrix A and let G be its comple-\nment, with adjacency matrix A. Then the spectrum spec(G) of G is the set of all eigenval-\nues of A, with corresponding multiplicities. It has been a longstanding problem to charac-\nterize graphs that are determined by their spectrum, that is to say: If spec(H) = spec(G),\ndoes it follow that H is isomorphic to G? If this is the case then G is determined by its\nspectrum, or a DS graph for short. In [4, 8, 9] it is conjectured that almost all graphs are\nDS, more recent surveys can be found in [5].\nA variant of this problem concerns the generalized spectrum of G which is given by the\npair\n\u0000\nspec(G), spec(G)\n\u0001\n. In this situation G is said to be determined by its generalized\nspectrum, or a DGS graph for short, if\n\u0000\nspec(H), spec(H)\n\u0001\n=\n\u0000\nspec(G), spec(G)\n\u0001\nimplies\nthat H is isomorphic to G. For the most recent results on DGS graphs see [13] and [20] in\nparticular. To date only a few families of graphs are known to be DS or DGS. This includes\nsome almost complete graphs [1], pineapple graphs [10] and kite graphs [11]. These are all\nknown to be DS, and in particular DGS. In addition, all rose graphs are determined by\ntheir Laplacian spectrum except for two speciﬁc examples, see [12].\nIn this paper we construct inﬁnite sequences of DGS graphs from certain small starter\ngraphs. This construction involves the walk matrix of a graph and recent results in [20].\nLet n be the number of vertices of G and let e be the column vector of height n with all\nentries equal to 1. Then the walk matrix of G is the n × n matrix\nW =\n\u0002\ne, Ae, A2e, · · · , An−1e\n\u0003\nDate: Version 3 September 2018, printed January 14, 2019.\n1Keywords: Graph spectrum, Walk matrix, Graphs determined by generalized spectrum\nMathematics Subject Classification: 05C50, 15A18\n1--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe (Generalized) Orthogonality Dimension of (https://golovnev.org/papers/kneser.pdf)\nciteturn1search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Note that the multichromatic numbers can be deﬁned in terms of Kneser graphs, namely, χk(G) is ... recently, it was related to the well-known recently disproved Hedetniemi’s conjecture [40]. ... ertheless, more than forty years since it was proposed, Stahl’s conjecture is still open.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the spectral characterization of Kite graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01632)\nciteturn1academia18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11.4 years ago; Let $G$ be a graph which is cospectral with $Kite_{p,q}$ and the clique number of $G$ is denoted by $w(G)$. ... Also, we prove that $Kite_{p,2}$ graphs are determined by their adjacency spectrum.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPacking chromatic number conjecture for 0-saturated subcubic graphs | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/373854/packing-chromatic-number-conjecture-for-0-saturated-subcubic)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # Packing chromatic number conjecture for 0-saturated subcubic graphs\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStahl’s Multichromatic Kneser-Graph Conjecture | ProofAtlas (https://www.proofatlas.ai/collaboration/stahl-multichromatic-kneser-graph-conjecture/)\nciteturn1sea